INSERT INTO feature VALUES('implicit-arguments','checking','Implicit arguments',NULL,'partial','ordinary',NULL,'Arguments the checker supplies through a prefix telescope, contextual metavariables and a spine pass. Rung A landed: implicits declared in one [...] prefix block, the core telescope interleaved by dependency, supply by name or by position through the slot (f[.i = e], f[e]), a standing supply. A printed call supplies by position each atom at the head of the written block, and the rest by name (#6320). Rung B landed: the solver (#1213) binds a contextual metavariable only where an equation forces a most general solution, postponing every other equation in one store by reason and blockers and refuting only a clash of introduction forms or a strongly rigid occurrence; the spine pass (#1216) makes each implicit a call omits a hole the call nominates, declared at the call''s binders, bound by the comparison that decodes it, and supplied in the body the checker emits, so the kernel never meets a metavariable. An implicit nothing forces is refused ImplicitUnsolved with the solver''s reason, and two arguments disagreeing on one are a type mismatch. An endpoint stuck on an implicit that an argument binds is read through the solution, so `ap f p` checks at `Path(f a, f b)` (#5480). Conversion pairs the fields of two applications of one constructor, and two different constructors are apart, so an implicit under a constructor in an index meets the field at its place: `head(pair())` binds `n` at `Succ(Zero)` (#3516). A recursive definition takes the prefix block too, def rec f [a : Type] (...) (#3828): its recursive call omits each implicit, one before the fixpoint passing the function''s own, so the call descends on the parameter its cases match. Rung C remains.','core-term surface-lowering core-unify core-checker surface-pretty surface-diagnostics','corpus/classifier/implicit-telescope.gandr corpus/pathological/classifier/implicit-telescope.gandr corpus/model/data/recursive-nat-lists.gandr corpus/pathological/data/dependent-vectors.gandr crates/core-unify/tests/solve.rs crates/core-checker-bridge/src/bridge/tests.rs::an_omitted_implicit_is_supplied_before_the_kernel_1216 crates/core-checker-bridge/src/bridge/tests.rs::an_endpoint_over_a_bound_implicit_reads_its_solution_5480 crates/surface-pretty/tests/goldens.rs::a_call_supplies_its_callee_s_implicits_by_position_6320','corpus/ledger/features/implicit-arguments.gandr','#315');
